The makela@tukki.jyu.fi (Otto J. Makela) writes:
-=> A floating eye should not be able to hold you under it's spell more than
-=> 2-3 turns AFTER it has been killed.  I find it very silly to get killed
-=> by walking at a E, having my dog kill it and THEN having the Orc band
-=> materialize around me (while still being held by the 20 turns dead Eye).

Floating eyes have been toned down a little.  It's also harder to run
into one accidentally, because the fast movement commands [the mMgG
prefixes, or using shift/control-[yuhjklbn] if the "number_pad" option
is not set (which addition i'm particularly proud of)] are "safe" now,
they won't attack a monster you run into.

-=> Does 2.3e still crash if a friendly long worm (like your polymorphed dog)
-=> tries to follow you up/down the stairs ?  Fix it at least in 3.0...

Long worms don't fit in stairways now.

-=> More INTERESTING (if hardly useful) things in the game.  I can't think
-=> of anything more useless than the sinks (yes I know, everything and the
-=> kitchen sink...), but they are hardly interesting either.

Sinks are a little more interesting now that you can drink from them.
Sort of mini-fountains, in a fashion.

There are several new items in the game, altho several of them are not
very interesting in my opionion.  5 different forms of shields, for
instance.  Some of the new magic items, however, are different from
anything you've seen in previous versions.

New things will probably not get in 3.0, but perhaps 3.1...

-=> Krazy glue traps (make wielded things stick to your hands temporarily,
-=> make YOU stick to the floor/walls, make the little dog stick to you...)
-=> The orc hits you --more--
-=> The orc sticks to you --more--
-=> You both collapse

More likely stuck monsters would be implemented like mimics- you can't
move away from them.  It's a bit silly, but it could be made to fit
the game mechanics.

-=> Laughing gas/tear gas traps (bring all monsters around, but make them also
-=> fall down laughing/crying helplessly).
-=> Boom!  A laughing gas trap blows up --more--
-=> Ha Ha Ha.  The gnome hits you --more--
-=> Ha Ha Ha.  The gnome starts laughing also --more--
-=> Ha Ha Ha.  You hit the laughing gnome

Then there's the implementation questions of which monsters laff.  Acid
blobs wouldn't, nymphs would, would dragons roar with laughter?

-=> Brine potions seem a viable idea.  Sure-fire (!) vomiting if you drink it,
-=> could #dip dead things in it to preserve them.  What about blinding Eyes
-=> with them ?
-=> The brine potion hits the floating eye --more--
-=> The eye closes

My image of the floating eye never included a membrane, but eyes can
be blinded.  It has possibilities.  It shouldn't be worth much in
shops.  It might even look like and be easy to confuse with the
potions of water we have now.

-=> Bring INTEREST in the game, the game difficulty level seems OK at
-=> the current level -- there are about as much people asking for a
-=> easier game as there are people to make it more difficult.

I disagree about the difficulty.  There were many features, and
several bugs, in 2.3 that could be easily abused.  And the wiz was a
wimp.  2.3 didn't require as much skill.  3.0 monsters are more
resourceful and more dangerous, but you can still defend yourself
(unlike the 2.3 black dragon, for which there are defenses in 3.0).


